{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Camera Principal Point.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Camera Principal Point.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"camera principal point camera principal point","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Camera Principal Point.md","fileName":"Camera Principal Point.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Camera Principal Point","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 00:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Photogrammetric Image Analysis]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Photogrammetric Image Analysis","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Camera Principal Point.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Camera Principal Point.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"camera principal point camera principal point","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Camera Principal Point.md","fileName":"Camera Principal Point.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Camera Principal Point","heading":"Camera Principal Point","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The camera principal point is where the optical axis intersects the image sensor, usually near the image center. Three vanishing points produced by mutually perpendicular scene directions form a triangle whose orthocenter identifies the principal point under the pinhole model.\n\nBecause an image has only one principal point, independent orthogonal structures should agree on its location. Inconsistent estimates can reveal composited geometry, while uncertain perpendicularity, lens distortion, or cropping must be accounted for before drawing that conclusion.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Photogrammetric Image Analysis","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Camera Principal Point.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Camera Principal Point.md","sour